WEBVTT

welcome-1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.769
Hello Chloe.

welcome-2
00:00:00.769 --> 00:00:06.154
This video helps you get ready for your knee arthroscopy (left knee) at Brackenridge.

welcome-3
00:00:06.154 --> 00:00:08.077
It takes about two minutes.

welcome-4
00:00:08.077 --> 00:00:13.462
You can pause it, turn on captions, or ask a question at any time.

what-happens-1
00:00:13.462 --> 00:00:21.154
Keyhole surgery: a small camera and instruments are passed through tiny cuts to look inside and repair your knee joint.

what-happens-2
00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:23.846
You'll be fully asleep during the procedure.

what-happens-3
00:00:23.846 --> 00:00:28.462
It's a day case, so you should go home the same day.

when-where-1
00:00:28.462 --> 00:00:31.154
Your appointment is on Thursday 19 November.

when-where-2
00:00:31.154 --> 00:00:32.692
Please arrive at 7am.

when-where-3
00:00:32.692 --> 00:00:36.923
Go to the Day Surgery Unit, Level 2, Brackenridge General Hospital.

when-where-4
00:00:36.923 --> 00:00:40.385
Expect to be with us for about 6 hours.

eating-drinking-1
00:00:40.385 --> 00:00:43.077
This part is important for your safety.

eating-drinking-2
00:00:43.077 --> 00:00:46.154
Don't eat anything after 2am on the day.

eating-drinking-3
00:00:46.154 --> 00:00:50.000
You can drink clear fluids until 6am on the day.

eating-drinking-4
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.923
After that, nothing at all.

eating-drinking-5
00:00:51.923 --> 00:00:57.692
If you eat or drink after these times, we may have to cancel your procedure.

medicines-1
00:00:57.692 --> 00:00:58.846
Now, your medicines.

medicines-2
00:00:58.846 --> 00:01:04.231
Take your usual morning medicines with a small sip of water, unless told otherwise.

medicines-3
00:01:04.231 --> 00:01:07.692
If you take blood-thinning medicines, call the pre-assessment team.

medicines-4
00:01:07.692 --> 00:01:10.000
Do not stop them without advice.

what-to-bring-1
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.769
Please bring a list of your medicines, loose shorts or trousers and flat, comfortable shoes.

what-to-bring-2
00:01:15.769 --> 00:01:18.077
Leave jewellery and valuables at home.

going-home-1
00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:24.615
You must have a responsible adult to take you home and stay with you for 24 hours.

going-home-2
00:01:24.615 --> 00:01:29.231
Do not drive until you can do an emergency stop without pain.

going-home-3
00:01:29.231 --> 00:01:32.692
For most people this is 1 to 2 weeks.

going-home-4
00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:35.000
Keep your leg raised when resting.

going-home-5
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.231
Most people return to desk work within 1 to 2 weeks.

warning-signs-1
00:01:39.231 --> 00:01:51.154
After you get home, call us straight away if you have any of these: increasing redness, heat or swelling around the knee; a high temperature; pain or swelling in your calf.

warning-signs-2
00:01:51.154 --> 00:01:55.000
Call 999 if you have chest pain or sudden breathlessness.

contact-1
00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:02.692
If you have a question, type it in the box next to this video, or call us on 01632 960577.

contact-2
00:02:02.692 --> 00:02:05.000
Outside office hours, call 01632 960999.

contact-3
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.692
We look forward to seeing you, Chloe.
